    "reason": "Pin the exact Windows/Linux runtime artifacts and narrow the source/publishing/native-notice boundary for the five remaining native-bearing TensorFlow/Keras direct dependencies. NumPy is refreshed from the historical lock's 2.1.3 to 2.4.6 because 2.4.6 remains compatible with Python 3.11 and TensorFlow's numpy >=1.26.0 constraint while adding current PyPI Trusted Publishing provenance and a verified upstream signed release tag. ml-dtypes 0.5.1 also has Trusted Publishing provenance, but its wheel disclosures require preserving Eigen's MPL-2.0 notice. grpcio 1.71.0, h5py 3.13.0 and libclang 18.1.1 have exact platform wheel identities but do not provide PyPI Trusted Publishing provenance for the selected files; h5py bundles HDF5 and libclang bundles a native libclang library. Execution therefore remains fail-closed until exact artifact-to-source/native notice closure is complete."
